+            // scRGB uses extended-range linear values (including values above
+            // 1.0 and below 0.0), which UNORM swapchains clip. On Wayland,
+            // externally managed color surfaces deliberately request the
+            // PASS_THROUGH colorspace using an UNKNOWN transfer function, so
+            // prefer float for that case as well. Normal fallback scoring is
+            // retained if no float surface is available.
+            if ((hint->transfer == PL_COLOR_TRC_SCRGB ||
+                 hint->transfer == PL_COLOR_TRC_UNKNOWN) &&
